  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Hedaol B and SK-VLB, mediated through the target SQ20B. Both Hedaol B and SQ20B are involved in the inhibition of SK-VLB, with SQ20B being a direct target of multiple compounds, including (R)-b-(Boc-amino)-2,5-difluorobenzenebutanoic acid and [(1R,2R,3R,5S,6R,9R,10R,11R,13S,14S,19S)-19-acetyloxy-2,5,10,11-tetrahydroxy-6,9,13-trimethyl-12-oxo-7,17-dioxapentacyclo[11.6.0.03,9.06,10.016,19]nonadecan-14-yl] acetate. This suggests that Hedaol B may act through a similar mechanism, possibly by binding to SQ20B and inhibiting its activity, which in turn affects SK-VLB. The final scores from the paths indicate a consistent and plausible relationship, though the exact mechanism of Hedaol B's interaction with SQ20B remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Hedaol B and SK-VLB, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the specific mode of action.",
